/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.1 Historical Milestones and Foundations of Electronics) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Electronics and Communication Engineering \(ECE\) is the engineering discipline that) Tj
T*
(harnesses the controlled motion of electrons and electromagnetic waves to process) Tj
T*
(information, communicate globally, and automate physical systems:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Pre-Semiconductor Era \(Late 19th - Early 20th Century\):) Tj
T*
(- James Clerk Maxwell \(1865\): Formulated electromagnetic theory, predicting that light) Tj
T*
(is an electromagnetic wave.) Tj
T*
(- Heinrich Hertz \(1887\): Experimentally verified Maxwell's equations using spark-gap) Tj
T*
(transmitters and receivers.) Tj
T*
(- Guglielmo Marconi \(1895-1901\): Pioneered long-distance wireless telegraphy,) Tj
T*
(transmitting transatlantic radio signals.) Tj
T*
(- John Ambrose Fleming \(1904\): Invented the Thermionic Diode \(Fleming Valve\), enabling) Tj
T*
(signal rectification.) Tj
T*
(- Lee de Forest \(1906\): Added a third control grid to create the Audion \(Triode vacuum) Tj
T*
(tube\), providing the first electronic signal amplification.) Tj
T*
(* 2. The Solid-State Revolution \(1947 - Present\):) Tj
T*
(- John Bardeen, Walter Brattain, and William Shockley \(Bell Labs, Dec 1947\): Invented) Tj
T*
(the Point-Contact Bipolar Transistor. Won the 1956 Nobel Prize in Physics. Transistors) Tj
T*
(completely replaced bulky, fragile, power-hungry vacuum tubes.) Tj
T*
(- Jack Kilby \(Texas Instruments, 1958\) & Robert Noyce \(Fairchild, 1959\): Co-invented the) Tj
T*
(Integrated Circuit \(IC\), integrating multiple transistors, resistors, and capacitors) Tj
T*
(onto a single semiconductor crystal slice.) Tj
T*
(- Intel 4004 \(1971\): First single-chip commercial microprocessor \(2,300 transistors, 10) Tj
T*
(um process\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 1.2 Moore's Law and Semiconductor Scaling) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Moore's Law \(Gordon Moore, 1965\): An empirical observation that the number of) Tj
T*
(transistors packed onto a dense microchip doubles approximately every 18 to 24) Tj
T*
(months, with a proportional decline in cost per transistor.) Tj
T*
(* Scaling Eras:) Tj
T*
(- Dennard Scaling Era \(1974-2005\): As transistors shrunk, power density remained) Tj
T*
(constant because operating voltage scaled down with dimensions. Allowed higher clock) Tj
T*
(frequencies \(up to ~3 GHz\).) Tj
T*
(- Multi-Core Era \(2005-Present\): Dennard scaling broke down due to subthreshold leakage) Tj
T*
(currents. Chip designers pivoted from pure clock speed to multi-core parallel) Tj
T*
ET

