([CASE STUDY 2: Moore's Law Physical Scaling Limits and 3D GAAFET Solutions]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Context: Analyze why traditional planar MOSFET scaling terminated at 20 nm and how 3D) Tj
T*
(transistor architectures rescued semiconductor progress.) Tj
T*
(Technical Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Short-Channel Effects in Planar MOSFETs: Below 20 nm channel length, the drain) Tj
T*
(electric field begins to control the channel conduction rather than the gate) Tj
T*
(\("Drain-Induced Barrier Lowering" - DIBL\). Subthreshold leakage currents surge) Tj
T*
(exponentially, causing excessive power dissipation even when the transistor is turned) Tj
T*
(OFF \(Dark Silicon phenomenon\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. The 3D FinFET Solution \(Intel 2011, TSMC\): The conducting channel is extruded) Tj
T*
(vertically as a thin 3D silicon "fin". The gate wraps around three sides of the fin) Tj
T*
(\(tri-gate\). This 3-sided electrostatic control dramatically tightens channel) Tj
T*
(pinch-off and suppresses leakage.) Tj
T*
(* 3. The Gate-All-Around \(GAAFET / Nanosheet\) Architecture: At sub-3nm nodes, FinFETs) Tj
T*
(encounter quantum tunneling limits. GAAFETs stack horizontal silicon nanosheets) Tj
T*
(vertically, with the gate material completely surrounding all four sides of each) Tj
T*
(nanosheet, achieving ultimate electrostatic gate control.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
