T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Context: Walk through the rigorous 9-stage engineering lifecycle of designing an) Tj
T*
(Application-Specific Integrated Circuit \(ASIC\) from concept to silicon tape-out.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step ASIC Engineering Lifecycle:) Tj
T*
(* Stage 1 \(Product Specification\): Define chip architecture, throughput, power) Tj
T*
(budget, clock frequencies, and interface protocols.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 2 \(RTL Design\): Hardware behavior authored in Verilog, SystemVerilog, or VHDL) Tj
T*
(using synthesizable register-transfer-level constructs.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 3 \(Functional Verification\): Extensive testbench creation using Universal) Tj
T*
(Verification Methodology \(UVM\) and constrained-random stimulus to achieve 100% code) Tj
T*
(and functional coverage.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 4 \(Logic Synthesis\): Synthesis tools \(Synopsys Design Compiler\) transform RTL) Tj
T*
(code into a gate-level netlist mapped to targeted foundry standard cells.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 5 \(Static Timing Analysis - STA\): Verify that all setup and hold timing) Tj
T*
(constraints are met across all process, voltage, and temperature \(PVT\) corners.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 6 \(Design for Testability - DFT\): Insert scan chains, boundary scan \(JTAG\),) Tj
T*
(and Built-In Self-Test \(BIST\) circuitry to enable automated post-fabrication silicon) Tj
T*
(defect testing.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 7 \(Physical Design - Place & Route\): Floorplanning, power mesh grid design,) Tj
T*
(clock tree synthesis \(CTS\), and signal routing using tools like Cadence Innovus.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 8 \(Physical Verification\): Design Rule Checking \(DRC\) and Layout Versus) Tj
T*
(Schematic \(LVS\) verification to guarantee layout matches electrical netlist without) Tj
T*
(geometric violations.) Tj
T*
(* Stage 9 \(Tape-Out\): Generation of GDSII / OASIS mask files sent to semiconductor) Tj
T*
(foundry \(e.g. TSMC, GlobalFoundries\) for wafer photolithography.) Tj
T*
